From: Daryl Denson <9751141+denson9874@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:54:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] cheetah: values stock sets that our build left at the
 AOSP default

A stock-vs-build comparison of every static overlay's values (stock
CP3A.261005.002.A1 against the target packages' effective values in our
build) found these left at the AOSP default. Each overlay copies stock's
values from its APKs (rro2xml.py), priority 1:
- framework: pin the camera app, compile Play Store in pre-reboot dexopt's
  synchronous phase, update the operator name once the carrier config has
  loaded, and Play Protect's dynamic instrumentation consumer (OdadPrebuilt)
- SystemUI: the screenshot Edit button opens Markup, the Files button opens
  Files by Google, Quick Share copy, the avatar picker we ship
  (com.google.android.avatarpicker, not com.android.avatarpicker), and Google
  Home first in device controls
- Settings: Google search and TalkBack slices, network list aggregation
- Wi-Fi: stock's 5 GHz scoring thresholds (bad -80, entry -77; AOSP -90/-85
  kept a weak 5 GHz network much longer)
- Connectivity: actively prefer a bad Wi-Fi network, as stock
- Photo picker: Google Photos as the cloud media provider

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
